{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Heard</b> — Some say: all <i>elohim</i> are the angels." "And the meaning of <b>bowed down to Him</b> — to give thanks, because all idol-worshippers were ashamed." "<b>And Zion rejoiced</b> — for there the glory was seen in the manifestation of His judgments; then it is proven — <b>for You are Most High above all <i>elohim</i></b> — in heaven and on earth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 97, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:28.988685182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}